WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.845
Six phases.

00:00:01.795 --> 00:00:04.681
Three hundred and forty emails tracked.

00:00:04.681 --> 00:00:09.340
One hundred and thirteen clean MPs with an accountability score of zero.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:12.204
Nine priority targets identified.

00:00:12.204 --> 00:00:17.056
This is the political accountability campaign — and every phase is documented.

00:00:17.056 --> 00:00:19.034
Phase One — Seed.

00:00:19.034 --> 00:00:24.874
Four media targets: CJPME, the Western Standard, Read the Maple, and Esprit de Corps.

00:00:24.874 --> 00:00:28.295
Get the story into outlets that will actually publish it.

00:00:28.295 --> 00:00:30.477
Phase Two — Recruit.

00:00:30.477 --> 00:00:35.988
Nine priority MPs plus one hundred and thirteen clean MPs across all parties.

00:00:35.988 --> 00:00:37.954
Cross-party alignment.

00:00:37.954 --> 00:00:39.988
This is not partisan.

00:00:39.988 --> 00:00:44.136
Phase Three — Arm. Party-specific accountability preparation.

00:00:44.136 --> 00:00:46.181
Phase Four — Pressure.

00:00:46.181 --> 00:00:52.715
Trigger committee studies at ETHI — the Ethics Committee — and NDDN — the National Defence Committee.

00:00:52.715 --> 00:00:55.795
Force the evidence onto the parliamentary record.

00:00:55.795 --> 00:00:57.863
Phase Five — Trap.

00:00:57.863 --> 00:01:00.465
Five Private Members' Bills queued.

00:01:00.465 --> 00:01:02.568
Legislation drafted.

00:01:02.568 --> 00:01:04.284
Ready to file.

00:01:04.284 --> 00:01:06.397
Phase Six — Close.

00:01:06.397 --> 00:01:08.829
Five-wall strategic closure.

00:01:08.829 --> 00:01:10.443
Parliamentary.

00:01:10.443 --> 00:01:11.749
Legal.

00:01:11.749 --> 00:01:13.159
Media.

00:01:13.159 --> 00:01:14.454
Public.

00:01:14.454 --> 00:01:16.090
International.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:18.045
Every exit blocked.

00:01:18.045 --> 00:01:20.545
Every escape route documented.

00:01:20.545 --> 00:01:24.170
Three Bloc Québécois kingmakers hold the balance of power.

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:28.124
Yves-François Blanchet, Claude Thériault, and Kristina Michaud.

00:01:28.124 --> 00:01:31.954
In a minority parliament, three votes can bring down a government.

00:01:31.954 --> 00:01:34.886
This campaign knows where those votes are.
